      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Part 2 of 3: Log the request and stand in for approval\n**Employee Request and Approval Router**\n\n1. Log Request: saves every request into a Data Table with its status set to Pending. The `employee_requests` Data Table is created for you automatically when n8n starts, so there is nothing to upload.\n\n2. Simulated Wait: pauses for a few seconds. In a real build, this is where an email goes out to the approver and the workflow waits for their click, which needs a working email credential.\n\n3. Auto-Approve (Demo): automatically marks the request approved after the wait, in the exact shape the real approval step would have produced, so the rest of the workflow runs exactly the same either way.\n\nWhy it is built this way: connecting a real inbox live, for everyone in the room, would eat the whole session on one login screen. This way you still build and run the full shape of the workflow today. Swapping in a real Gmail, Outlook, or Slack 'Send and Wait' node here later takes only a few minutes, and nothing downstream needs to change.\n\nImport part 3 next and connect Auto-Approve (Demo) into Is Approved?.",
        "width": 680,
        "height": 560
      }
    }
  ],
